    "q-141984": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141984",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${({a}^{2}b)}^{3}\\cdot ab=$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({a}^{2}b)}^{3}\\cdot ab=({a}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {b}^{3}\\cdot ab & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({a}^{2})^{3}\\cdot {b}^{3}\\cdot ab & = \\\\ {a}^{2\\cdot 3}\\cdot {b}^{3}\\cdot ab & = \\\\ {a}^{6}\\cdot {b}^{3}\\cdot ab & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{6}\\cdot {b}^{3}\\cdot ab & = \\\\ ({a}^{6}\\cdot a)\\cdot ({b}^{3}\\cdot b) & = \\\\ {a}^{6+1}\\cdot {b}^{3+1} & = \\\\ {a}^{7}\\cdot {b}^{4} & = \\\\ {a}^{7}{b}^{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
