    "q-2629": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2629",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\frac{100{x}^{7}{y}^{3}}{20{x}^{3}{y}^{2}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We separate the fraction, group the two variables separately, and apply the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{100{x}^{7}{y}^{3}}{20{x}^{3}{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{100}{20}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{7}}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}} & = \\\\ 5\\cdot {x}^{(7-3)}\\cdot {y}^{(3-2)} & = \\\\ 5{x}^{4}{y}^{1} & = \\\\ 5{x}^{4}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
