    "q-22838": {
      "dom_id": "step-q22838",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to ${(\\frac{{u}^{2}}{-2{v}^{4}})}^{5}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by using the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{{u}^{2}}{-2{v}^{4}})}^{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{{({u}^{2})}^{5}}{{(-2{v}^{4})}^{5}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule in the numerator and the power of product rule in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{({u}^{2})}^{5}}{{(-2{v}^{4})}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{u}^{2\\cdot 5}}{(-2)^{5}\\cdot {({v}^{4})}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{u}^{10}}{(-2)^{5}\\cdot {({v}^{4})}^{5}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the power rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{u}^{10}}{(-2)^{5}\\cdot {({v}^{4})}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{u}^{10}}{(-2)^{5}\\cdot {v}^{4\\cdot 5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{u}^{10}}{(-32)\\cdot {v}^{20}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{{u}^{10}}{32{v}^{20}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
