    "q-142145": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142145",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\sqrt[4]{y}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the radical as a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\sqrt[4]{y}={y}^{1/2}\\cdot {y}^{1/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{1/2}\\cdot {y}^{1/4} & = \\\\ {y}^{1/2+1/4} & = \\\\ {y}^{3/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we express the result as a radical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3/4} & =\\sqrt[4]{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
